<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Casa da Índia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Casa da Índia was the royal trading house in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> that managed the crown monopoly over spice imports from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> in the sixteenth century. It organised fleets, collected goods and redistributed them to European markets. It functioned as the commercial nerve centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/casa-da-india.jpg" alt="Casa da Índia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nuno Tavares · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Casa_da_Guin%C3%A9.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
